(FIL-02: descriptor is a Number. Its exact value depends on what else is
 open, so the floor is taken from an anchor handle opened first and kept
 open: a freshly opened handle must report a descriptor greater than the
 anchor's, since a descriptor still in use is never handed out again.
 The floor is not "at least 3". Descriptors 0 to 2 are only taken while
 the standard streams stay open; FUZZER_DEFECTS.md Defect 27 was a
 program that closed a borrowed descriptor 0 first. Run once by hand
 with `open a file for reading called keyboard at 0.` and
 `Close keyboard.` added before the anchor, the anchor got 0, the
 handle under test got 3, and the check passed. That variant is not
 retained, because its output depends on what Close does to a borrowed
 descriptor, which the manual does not yet say.
 Also covers: FIL-01 (size is 0 before a write and the byte count after,
 checked BEFORE Close - reading a property after Close reports -1, not
 the true value, which is why every assertion here happens on the open
 handle).
 This is the exact assertion SHAPE the leaf renders: `If <bad> then,
 Print "ASSERT <ID>: ...", Exit 95. Print <subject>` - not just the raw
 value, the failing branch too (proven by the deliberately-broken run
 below).
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/var/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /var/home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-02.vox -o p && ./p
 on vox main a0a2ecc.
 With the descriptor check changed to `is greater than` (a deliberately
 wrong expectation), to prove a failing assertion is classified
 correctly, it printed `ASSERT FIL-02: expected greater than 3 got 4`
 and exited 95.
 actual output:
   0
   4
   10
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called 'the drawer' at "vf_scratch/files/fil02.txt".
open a file for writing called 'the toolbox' at "vf_scratch/files/fil02.txt".
If 'the toolbox's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-01: expected 0 got {'the toolbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the toolbox's size.
If 'the toolbox's descriptor is less than or equal to 'the drawer's descriptor then, Print "ASSERT FIL-02: expected greater than {'the drawer's descriptor} got {'the toolbox's descriptor}", Exit 95. Print 'the toolbox's descriptor.
Write "seed bytes" to 'the toolbox'.
If 'the toolbox's size is not 10 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-01: expected 10 got {'the toolbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the toolbox's size.
Close 'the toolbox'.
Close 'the drawer'.
